      "message": "﻿ci(release): a site_only dispatch can take the app of an earlier run\n\nA site_only dispatch skips the wasm job, so the site goes out with app/\nas its \"not part of this copy\" page. The new optional dispatch input\napp_run_id names an earlier run (the release's tag run). With site_only,\nthe site job downloads that run's wasm-app artifact (run-id, job token,\nactions: read) and checks it with web/check-app-page.sh. On this path a\nfailed download or check fails the job, so nothing deploys. The tag\npath, a plain dispatch and site_only without the input are unchanged.\n\nRefs #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
